          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "آواز خواندن (âvâz khândan) — \"to sing\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مادرم در آشپزخانه آواز میخواند. mâdaram dar âshpazkhâne âvâz mikhânad. My mother sings in the kitchen."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "âvâz 'song, voice' + khândan 'to read, to sing'; present stem khân-."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "âvâz is inherited: EtymDB traces it to a Middle Persian word for 'voice, sound, tune' and lists Latin vōx, 'voice', as a cousin (EtymDB). khândan is inherited too."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
